            <ArticleTitle>[Acute calcific prevertebral tendinitis: case report and literature review].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>389-92</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.recot.2012.05.009</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Prevertebral calcific tendinitis is an uncommon cause of acute neck pain characterized by the identification of calcifications at C1-C2 level and the presence of a liquid collection at the prevertebral space which causes the displacement of the prevertebral radiographic line in imaging studies. It is very important to identify this rare, benign and self-limiting pathology, in order not to confuse it with other diseases that could erroneously lead to inappropriate treatment.</AbstractText>
